In 1D everything should be fine, but I think with thousands of these
logistics distributions you can get “corners” in the typical set that
might occasional trap the chains.  But this is just pondering — more
work is needed to dig into what’s happening.  I recommend looking
at the n_leapfrog distributions for each chain, finding the slow ones,
and comparing them to the fast chains.

