Subject: Re: Parser Warning from Double For Loop
Message-ID: <yGZXAtk7rac.1PCiTi8ZDwAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <yGZXAtk7rac.RhiYjxIUDwAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
References: <yGZXAtk7rac.RhiYjxIUDwAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/yGZXAtk7rac/m/1PCiTi8ZDwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This might be as simple as switching from "=" to "<-" for assignment. I don't think we introduced "=" for assignment until version 2.10, so if you're running 2.9.x then the problem might just be that

 epsilon[j,t] = ...

should be

 epsilon[j,t] <- ...

I haven't checked if there are other problems with the code but that would be the first thing to try I think.

Jonah

