I’ll also note that statistical models built out of inversions/decompositions
are almost always a mess to fit.  This can be explained by their compromising
the generative structure of the model, or just looking at how ill-posed the
gradients are.

> On Mar 13, 2017, at 8:43 PM, Ben Goodrich <goodri...@gmail.com> wrote:
