> Haha, agreed in my limited experience. I think we got pretty lucky with this model/data. I coded this up in Python with the 2012 Radford Neal HMC paper and things just kinda work, which is why I think there's a chance I could take advantage of all the nice Stan stuff if I can weasel it in. You're right though; it still feels like a coinflip.

You will likely find that “just kinda works” is really “works for
a small part of parameter space, preventing the sampler from
exploring all of the relevant parts of parameters space and
hence biasing inferences.”  Stan will certainly help you
diagnose such problems, but it won’t be able to fix them.

